# shell: desktop
# home: fixture
# prefs: factory
# A line of a program, coloured by what its parts MEAN -- end to end,
# through the application the person actually types into.
#
# The two pixels below were probed rather than guessed, and they are
# GLYPH pixels: the ink a letter is drawn with, not chrome.  Each is
# asserted twice, before and after, so what is proven is the CHANGE --
# this stretch of the line stopped being ordinary ink and became the
# shade the theme names for what it means.
wait 14
click 980 30
wait 4
menu-pick Applications
wait 4
menu-pick Editor
wait 90
expect-title Edit
note one line of TikuOS BASIC, typed into the editor a key at a time
key 1
wait 3
key 0
wait 3
key space
wait 3
key P
wait 3
key R
wait 3
key I
wait 3
key N
wait 3
key T
wait 3
key space
wait 3
key A
wait 12
shot /tmp/tiku-editor-plain.png
note until it is asked, the editor holds prose: every byte is the
note document's own ink, because a name that says nothing about the
note language is not a reason to colour anything
expect-pixel 267 145 080808
expect-pixel 299 145 000000
note the editor offers the choice by name, and the row says which way
note it goes -- a published row is a label and a command, and a
note checkmark would have to be invented in the wire as well
click 212 8
wait 6
expect-menu Colour as BASIC
menu-pick Colour as BASIC
wait 20
shot /tmp/tiku-editor-syntax.png
note now the line number stands back: ordinary ink pulled halfway to
note the page, which is the one derivation that survives a dark table
expect-pixel 267 145 838383
note and PRINT wears the shade the theme names for a word the
note language reserves -- taken from the interpreter's own table
expect-pixel 299 145 0000b0
note the row keeps ONE name and wears a mark while it holds, rather
note than renaming itself into what would read as a second command
click 212 8
wait 6
expect-menu Colour as BASIC
note and taking it again puts both stretches back to the document's own
note ink -- the claim a one-way toggle cannot make
menu-pick Colour as BASIC
wait 20
expect-pixel 267 145 080808
expect-pixel 299 145 000000
note and the editor is put away rather than left standing: a script
note that leaks a running application poisons the one after it.  Its
note tab first: the bar took the keyboard when its menu was opened, and
note a key aimed at an application has to be aimed at its window.
click-window Edit
wait 6
key Escape
wait 8
expect-title Edit
note Escape in the question presses Cancel, the safe road: still standing
key Escape
wait 6
expect-title Edit
note asked again, Return cancels; an explicit Discard click closes it
key Escape
wait 6
key Return
wait 8
expect-title Edit
key Escape
wait 6
click 592 318
wait 60
expect-no-title Edit
quit
